<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu'l-Futuh al-Hasan ibn Ja'far</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1039</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Abu'l-Futuh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu'l-Futuh al-Hasan ibn Ja'far was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharif-of-mecca">Sharif of Mecca</a> from about 994 to 1039. In 1011, encouraged by the Jarrahid chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mufarrij-ibn-daghfal">Mufarrij ibn Daghfal</a>, he was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> in opposition to the Fatimid caliph al-Hakim. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> won the Jarrahids back, he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and resumed recognising Fatimid authority.</p></div>
